I bought them for my wife as a gift, I knew with Teva I had assured durability and quality.She really liked the fit and the design...
I bought the Teva Women's Ventura Cork 2 Wedge Sandal in Ebony for $39.90 when it was offered during a Friday Sale. The sandal looks exactly like the pictures and is true to size. The cork sole provides good cushioning and keeps my feet comfortable walking on concrete all day. I also like the adjustability of the velcro strap closure.My only complaint is that the heel bed is a little long for my foot so the slope downward didn't hit my arch in the right spot (I have high arches). To solve this problem, I put in a pair of Dr. Scholl's For Her Comfort Insoles with clear massaging gel, which stay in place and provide some arch support as well as extra cushioning and, because they're clear, they can't be seen when I'm wearing the sandals. I read on another site that the stitching near the toes bothered a couple of people so I also put in a pair of ball-of-foot cushions which cover the stitching and provide extra cushioning.I probably wouldn't have paid full price for these sandals, but at $40 they're a real bargain if you're looking for a cute, sturdy, and comfortable pair of wedge sandals. If they came in red or beige like the lower heeled version, I would buy them in an instant.
